# mr

## Intent
Provide Pi-free, fakeable Effect services for reading and mutating an existing GitLab merge request, reading branch commits, and polling pipeline state.

## Contract
`MergeRequestService` exposes status, thread, reply, update, and pipeline operations. `MergeRequestCommitService` reads current-branch commits used for update derivation. `MergeRequestClock` and `MergeRequestTimer` keep time and sleeps replaceable in deterministic tests. Live layers expose only injected command-transport seams to the core. GitLab failures use `MergeRequestGitLabError`; commit-read failures use `MergeRequestCommitError`.

## Behaviour
1. GitLab status maps IID, title, draft, discussion state, pipeline state, unresolved count, and bound ticket.
2. Thread reads preserve author, bot, code position, body, and resolution metadata.
3. Reply and update operations remain explicit service calls.
4. Commit reads return subjects and bodies without reading package metadata.
5. Pipeline reads expose known states, map unsupported states to `unknown`, and are polled by the extension core through the timer seam until terminal.

## Edge cases
- Malformed or nonzero subprocess responses become typed lookup errors.
- Unknown pipeline values become `unknown`; absent code positions remain undefined.
- Missing bound tickets remain undefined.

## Non-goals
This module does not import Pi, register tools, own session timers, deliver follow-ups, create merge requests, or infer repository facts.

## Evidence
The colocated live boundary test injects command transport and verifies a read-only status payload is decoded into the typed merge request result and expected safe command request.

